whole screen as your hands-on agent. Subcommands when you want a specific blade:

  diablo train voice    pick a voice from the list, or add a new one; three spoken rounds
                        blended into it. Shows recordings and sessions per voice, before and after
  diablo -c             him again exactly where you left: the newest session of this folder
  diablo -r             the session picker, newest first, across every folder, enter to resume
  diablo train agent    he records his own voice, nobody else needed
  diablo reset voice    delete a named profile after confirmation
  diablo rename voice   give a profile a better name
  diablo test voice     live ranking of who the microphone hears, scored ten times a second,
                        smoothed bars with threshold and peak marks, a session summary on quit.
                        a plays his sample, q quits
  diablo tasks          his task board, the one source of truth: list, show, add, tell,
                        cancel, retry. --json on any of them for the dashboard and the panels.
                        diablo tasks help
  diablo talk           him in your terminal: type a line, he answers here and out loud,
                        worker starts and reports scroll by, /tasks shows the board
  diablo agent          him as your hands-on agent, like a butler in the editor's chair:
                        one session in your current directory, he reads, edits, runs and
                        checks with his own tools while you watch, /new and /brain inside
  diablo messages       login (telegram, once), check, read <chat>; his eyes on your chats
"""

